#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "52fc2fee-c015-55e0-b411-03c86d5992e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5447" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/e8a14ffbaab4597a2a4a7c9a6bad61dabbc4970fc22c3ed2eb28b2594a670938.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "8b7758b4-e0ec-5872-90d7-1136c9716574" :question/math-academy-id "e-6682" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baafa12f-49d2-5c88-8949-ad01d9c5840c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084622} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e832b2-3d84-5943-b50a-0ae01be865c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image