 $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(2,-3),(-2,1),(2,3)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4e456209fc818f606bfe83324b05843b0122840161a84a8d729927f4050f2397.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6f322ad-95a5-5c05-b401-86954c9727d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/02b7a778b46085876e5269e0b088dde52293d5230cd0312459ec21c8b2600f71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283468} {:answer/id #uuid "c784b9a6-3843-51dd-b0c0-04e05a66b725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/5485aedcf92aca355118c8bd051f16a1436d5f955a0dde65c85eaa0398eb03b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283469} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddaf679-ec51-59f2-8b9a-5528425d9db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283470} {:answer/id #uuid "a13f5005-67c7-58aa-ba32-b4b9e342f7ff" :answer/type {:db/ident 