 the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c1e596-f225-5afb-a879-564bc5a789dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283475} {:answer/id #uuid "dea2bf57-65e6-5ffb-9c4c-f7cd13b6eefa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dea2bf57-65e6-5ffb-9c4c-f7cd13b6eefa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283476} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb5b2820-0aaf-548a-978a-9ac1098f3657" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354bb4d6-72b6-5bdf-834a-4208ce5820ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "354bb4d6-72b6-5bdf-834a-4208ce5820ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283478} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d218b8a-89df-5784-aa5e-9c965cb9d980" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e300546a-b3a9-5328-900d-35daebc6283d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e300546a-b3a9-5328-900d-35daebc6283d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283480} :answer-field/id #uuid "4250aa27-770a-59a5-af77-28e44a405418" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8716484a-def2-5aad-88c9-6e1ad98f3304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8716484a-def2-5aad-88c9-6e1ad98f3304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05d1f78-0e9a-5806-9f31-e7262a625dbb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283481}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d99c7e0a-a02d-5d45-a6e5-6a400ff91985" :question/math-academy-id "q-281541" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the linear transformation with matrix representation $T$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{EF}$ has endpoints at $E(1,1)$ and $F(2,3).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{E}^{′}{F}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${E}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{F}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{EF}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{EF}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${E}^{′}(5,5)$ and ${F}^{′}(10,15).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df433510-1919-54ee-994a-7b458d1ec5fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df433510-1919-54ee-994a-7b458d1ec5fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283485} :answer-field/id #uuid "29185e37-a891-5c14-924d-fedd7a80640a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1246333-14e4-5a50-848e-76e5eabcca36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1246333-14e4-5a50-848e-76e5eabcca36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283487} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ff07c1-f276-5892-a28a-b1d580931063" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab15aa0b-3ce9-5114-908a-aac3772ea078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab15aa0b-3ce9-5114-908a-aac3772ea078" :answer/type {:db/ident :a