answer/id #uuid "e1507150-75a1-5489-9d64-fbd67e6521d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283517} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b58a64e-dae0-581a-b5f4-aad15f99bd80" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b25a6746-1764-58d6-ae86-0cdc2cbfa5a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-281566" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $PQR$ has vertices at $P(-2,2),\\,Q(2,3),$ and $R(0,-2).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$, the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${P}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{Q}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{R}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $△PQR$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 18 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(2,2),$\n${Q}^{′}(18,8),$ ${R}^{′}(-8,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{