nswer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1742b07-44a3-5a74-8a7a-20d14975ace1" :question/math-academy-id "q-77709" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fa8ce497e80e941730cebb8528b09725930fcb31c839ac0020ce7cf9f0a39b58.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(5,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dcfbb3e-ec5f-55a0-9495-fb6d6724d072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :an