tion/math-academy-id "q-77717" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fc7bebddc280debd4bde32393cabfa4a6a91a782d38e5406f374cc4eaa4ac68f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(5,7)$ and ${B}^{′}(-9,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/177ca7f40ef24cf2f45a15b78487700d1f0efd094c975079cf4704b46debefb1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a50a9e7-7fae-5138-a59d-bc35b4e16167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/0f5bf56cb4e4546079d89fd97b9533676116d4cff5435cbc926b925af5d3f637.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283541} {:answer/id #uuid 